# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Winternight Stories's post-draw discard —
#   DB$ Discard | Defined$ You | NumCards$ 2 | Mode$ TgtChoose | UnlessType$ Creature
#   — discard 2 cards, unless one of them is a creature, in which case a single
#   creature card is enough.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = the spell resolves and the discard is answered by a real client choice.
#   LOSE = the cast did not complete before the turn limit.
#   TIMEOUT = the discard prompt never receives a client response — the defect
#     this fixture guards: chooseCardsToDiscardUnlessType built its own bare
#     PromptRequest with no candidateRefs and the Generic semantic, which
#     resolves to no coordinator-owned runtime, so the choice was silently
#     auto-decided with no prompt ever reaching the client.
# Card roles:
#   Winternight Stories — draws 3, then exposes the unless-type discard.
#   Grizzly Bears — every card the draw can produce is a creature, so the
#     "unless" branch is reachable regardless of library draw order.
# Protocol path: Cast, ActionsAvailableReq, SelectNReq (discard).
[metadata]
Name:Winternight Stories Unless-Type Discard
Goal:Win
Turns:2
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Cast Winternight Stories, draw three, discard one creature to satisfy the unless clause.

